Advanced Hydraulics — Suresh A. Kartha (@fd-hydraulics: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_1MCV024RY5CA95WTHY708FP7VT
Suresh A. Kartha, IIT Guwahati. NPTEL Advanced Hydraulics, course 105103021. [Official course](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/105103021).

Work the complete open-channel progression: geometric and flow descriptions, energy and momentum, critical/uniform flow, gradually varied profiles, hydraulic jumps and surges, and channel transitions. The final machine lectures connect momentum principles with pumps, turbines and cavitation and can support the later engineering study.

The official indexed lecture inventory identifies these modules and the instructor. The live page can return a client-side loading shell to automated readers, so not every embedded lecture is claimed to have been played. Public course access is distinct from the terms of separate textbooks and current examination offerings. Keep lectures, notes and other media external and preserve their notices.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
